  "title": "Operator and device scanning workflow",
  "description": "A physical workflow with a location, a handheld device, a wrong-object operator error, and an offline queue whose application time the manual leaves undefined.",
  "files": {
    "requirements.md": "# Scanning workflow\n\n## RF-030 Scan an item into a bin\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- Scanning an item into a bin increases the bin count and records the scan event.\n\n## RF-031 Refuse an item that belongs to another bin\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n\n- Scanning an item that belongs to another bin is refused and the bin count is unchanged.\n",
    "device-manual.md": "# Device manual\n\nStep DEV-1: at the receiving station, wake the handheld scanner and open Scan to bin.\nStep DEV-2: scan the bin label, then scan the item label.\nStep DEV-3: an operator who scans an item belonging to another bin sees the scan refused.\nStep DEV-4: if the handheld loses network during a scan the screen shows Offline and the\nscan is queued. The manual does not state when the queued scan is applied.\n"
  },
